897	@@ -0,0 +1,153 @@
898	+# SMA-826 — Move the shared core test helpers into `tests/common`
899	+
900	+Size: a small change. Test-only. No public API, book or README change.
901	+
902	+## Intent
903	+
904	+Three core integration test files keep their own copies of the same test
905	+helpers. A change to one copy does not reach the other copies, and no test
906	+fails when they drift. SMA-810 changed the pairing oracle and had to change
907	+each copy by hand. After this change, each helper has one source in core.
908	+
909	+One copy of the oracle stays in runtime-tokio. No test catches drift between
910	+that copy and the core source. We accept this because a shared crate is out
911	+of scope. Doc comments in both directions name the other copy.
912	+
913	+## Current state (measured on `main` at `e7ac5377`)
914	+
915	+| Helper | Copies | Difference between copies |
916	+|---|---|---|
917	+| `assert_tool_calls_paired` | `tests/deferred_resume.rs:579`, `tests/handoff_transfer_result.rs:187`; runtime-tokio `tests/deferred.rs:427` | The code is equal in all three. Only comments differ. The `handoff_transfer_result.rs` doc comment has one more sentence about the round rule. The `deferred_resume.rs` and runtime-tokio copies have inline comments. |
918	+| `DeferB` | `tests/deferred_resume.rs:24`, `tests/handoff_transfer_result.rs:601`, `tests/subagent_propagation.rs:338` | The `subagent_propagation.rs` copy uses the prompt `"policy says wait"`; the other two use `"pay?"`. |
919	+| `RequestLog` | `tests/deferred_resume.rs:45`, `tests/handoff_transfer_result.rs:622` | None. |
920	+| `CapturingModel` (not named in the issue) | `tests/subagent_propagation.rs:359` | Same behaviour as `RequestLog`. It has no constructor and no `requests()` getter; the test reads the field directly. |
921	+
922	+`tests/common/mod.rs` already exists. 25 core test files include it with
923	+`#[path = "common/mod.rs"] mod common;`. It has `#![allow(dead_code, ...)]`, so
924	+a helper that one binary does not use causes no warning.
925	+
926	+## Goals
927	+
928	+- `assert_tool_calls_paired`, `DeferB` and `RequestLog` are `pub` items in
929	+  `crates/paigasus-helikon-core/tests/common/mod.rs`. The three test files
930	+  import them from `common` and keep no local copy.
931	+- `CapturingModel` in `subagent_propagation.rs` is removed. Its test uses
932	+  `RequestLog`.
933	+- Each test keeps its behaviour. `cargo test -p paigasus-helikon-core` passes,
934	+  and the test count of each changed test binary does not change.
935	+- The runtime-tokio copy of `assert_tool_calls_paired` gets a doc comment that
936	+  names `crates/paigasus-helikon-core/tests/common/mod.rs` as the source.
937	+
938	+## Non-goals
939	+
940	+- No shared crate between core and runtime-tokio (the issue excludes it).
941	+- No change to the runtime-tokio permission policies `DeferPolicy`
942	+  (`tests/deferred.rs:31`) and `DeferPay` (`tests/turn_checkpoint.rs:317`).
943	+  They defer the tool `pay`, so they are not copies of `DeferB`.
944	+- No `exclude = ["tests/"]` in a crate manifest. That changes the published
945	+  package contents and needs its own ticket.
946	+- No other test helper moves (for example `tool_result_texts`, `call_b_turn`).
947	+
948	+## Anti-goals
949	+
950	+- A changed oracle rule. The shared oracle must have the same code as the
951	+  current copies, character for character, apart from comments.
952	+
953	+## Approaches
954	+
955	+1. **Move into the existing `tests/common/mod.rs` (chosen).** The issue names
956	+   this module. All files already include it, and its `dead_code` allow
957	+   covers unused helpers.
958	+2. **A new submodule, for example `tests/common/deferral.rs`.** A
959	+   `pub mod deferral;` line in `mod.rs` would load it, so the 25 include
960	+   sites would not change. The issue names `mod.rs`, so this approach is not
961	+   used.
962	+3. **A shared dev-only crate for core and runtime-tokio.** The issue puts it
963	+   out of scope.
964	+4. **runtime-tokio includes the core file with a cross-crate `#[path]`.**
965	+   The path is outside the runtime-tokio package. Each crate publishes its
966	+   `tests/` directory, so the published runtime-tokio tests would not
967	+   compile. This approach is not used, and the runtime-tokio copy stays.
968	+
969	+## Design
970	+
971	+- **Oracle.** Move it into `common/mod.rs` with the fullest comments: the
972	+  `handoff_transfer_result.rs` doc comment (with the round-rule sentence)
973	+  and the inline comments of the `deferred_resume.rs` copy. The code does not
974	+  change. Add this text to its doc comment: "A copy is in
975	+  `crates/paigasus-helikon-runtime-tokio/tests/deferred.rs`. Keep the two
976	+  copies the same."
977	+- **Oracle self-test.** The `#[should_panic]` test
978	+  `pairing_oracle_rejects_a_call_after_a_result_while_a_call_waits` stays in
979	+  `deferred_resume.rs`. A `#[test]` in `common/mod.rs` would run once in each
980	+  of the 25 test binaries.
981	+- **`DeferB`.** Move it with the prompt `"pay?"`. *My call:* the
982	+  `subagent_propagation.rs` tests check only the prefix
983	+  `"permission denied: approval deferred, but this run cannot defer: "` with
984	+  `starts_with`, so the prompt text does not change what they check.
985	+- **`RequestLog`.** Move it with its `with_scripts` constructor and its
986	+  `requests()` getter. Both methods must be `pub fn`, because `common` is a
987	+  child module (a private method gives error E0624). The fields stay
988	+  private.
989	+- **`CapturingModel`.** *My call:* replace it with `RequestLog` in
990	+  `subagent_propagation.rs`. It is the same type of copy that the issue wants
991	+  to remove. The test then uses `RequestLog::with_scripts(...)` and
992	+  `.requests()` in place of the struct literal and the direct field read.
993	+- **Imports.** Add `PermissionDecision` and `PermissionPolicy` to
994	+  `common/mod.rs` (the others are already there). Remove the imports that
995	+  become unused. `cargo test` only warns on them; the clippy `-D warnings`
996	+  gate fails. The challenger worked out this list; clippy is the final check:
997	+  - `deferred_resume.rs`: remove `Model`, `ModelCapabilities`, `ModelError`.
998	+  - `handoff_transfer_result.rs`: remove `Mutex`, `PermissionDecision`,
999	+    `PermissionPolicy`.
1000	+  - `subagent_propagation.rs`: remove `BoxStream`, `CancellationToken`,
1001	+    `Model`, `ModelCapabilities`, `ModelError`, `ModelRequest`,
1002	+    `PermissionDecision`, `PermissionPolicy`.
1003	+- **runtime-tokio.** Replace the doc comment of
1004	+  `crates/paigasus-helikon-runtime-tokio/tests/deferred.rs:427` with the
1005	+  core doc comment, and change its pointer from `deferred_resume.rs` to
1006	+  `crates/paigasus-helikon-core/tests/common/mod.rs`. Keep the sentence
1007	+  "Keep the two copies the same." *My call:* remove "(pre-flight ruling F5)",
1008	+  because it refers to a SMA-803 working document that is not in the repo
1009	+  history a reader has. Its code does not change.
1010	+- **Commit type.** `test(core)` for the code, `docs(spec)` / `docs(plan)` for
1011	+  the design files. The PR title is `test(core): SMA-826 move the shared core
1012	+  test helpers into tests/common`.
1013	+
1014	+## Release
1015	+
1016	+`test(core)` does not stop a release. Neither crate manifest has `include`
1017	+or `exclude`, so `tests/` is in each published package. release-plz
1018	+attributes a bump by file path, and `.versionrc` controls only convco. Core
1019	+0.5.21 and 0.5.5 shipped from commits that were not `feat` or `fix`.
1020	+
1021	+So this PR makes release-plz propose a patch for core and runtime-tokio,
1022	+and `dependencies_update` cascades to the dependents and the facade. Keep
1023	+`test(core)`: it is the correct type, and it prevents a minor bump.
1024	+
1025	+The SMA-810 core patch (`e7ac5377`) is on `main` and is not released. Release
1026	+PR #357 carried it, but #357 was closed without a merge at 18:54 UTC on
1027	+2026-11-20, and no release PR is open. The next push to `main` makes
1028	+release-plz open a new release PR. If this PR merges before that release PR
1029	+merges, the test changes go into the same patch as SMA-810. If a release PR
1030	+merges first, this PR makes a release that holds only test changes. That is
1031	+harmless but noisy. The merge order is Sven's call.
1032	+
1033	+## Verification
1034	+
1035	+- Before and after the move, record `cargo test -p paigasus-helikon-core
1036	+  --test deferred_resume --test handoff_transfer_result --test
1037	+  subagent_propagation -- --list` and compare the test names.
1038	+- `cargo test -p paigasus-helikon-core` and
1039	+  `cargo test -p paigasus-helikon-runtime-tokio --test deferred` pass.
1040	+- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` and the workspace clippy gate pass.
1041	+- `grep -rnE '^(pub )?(struct (DeferB|RequestLog|CapturingModel)\b|fn assert_tool_calls_paired\b)' crates/paigasus-helikon-core/tests`
1042	+  gives three lines, all in `common/mod.rs`, and no `CapturingModel`.
1043	+- Diff the shared oracle against `git show main:crates/paigasus-helikon-core/tests/deferred_resume.rs`
1044	+  (lines 579-619). Only `pub` and the doc comment may differ. Diff the
1045	+  runtime-tokio function against the shared one. Only the doc comment and
1046	+  `pub` may differ.
1047	+
1048	+## Left to the builder
1049	+
1050	+- Where in `common/mod.rs` the helpers go (at the end is fine).
